    preserve density/units/noise/anchoring, source bounds, sample schedules, support, six-target OIT,
    physical encoding, history and resource ownership. Cache/detail/format/source-selection and
    control alternatives have explicit measured or contract-backed rejection/deferral. They are
    not delivered approximation changes. Phase 9, parent/reflection integration and user-run native
    appearance/whole-frame performance remain open; no headless result completes those gates.

Default internal shadow-cache enablement (2026-10-18)
  Explicit user direction supersedes the initial decision above to keep attenuation reuse opt-in.
  Production reduced tracing now builds and uses the selected source's same-frame cache by default.
  CloudShadowCache owns persistent 256x256 RGBA32F storage and a bounded 64-sample generation pass;
    existing map/root certification, physical inputs, typed shader/resource contracts and engine
    boundaries supply generation and submission. The other source, invalid/unavailable/unsupported
    data and full-resolution reference retain bounded secondary marching. Changed approximation is
    explicit: first/last occupied distance and integrated optical depth become a nearest-sampled
    mean-extinction interval. Native density, geometry, primary controls and OIT factors are unchanged.
  Ordinary draws rebuild before use, complete image/texture visibility barriers and revalidate the
    native borrow. Source-lifetime replacement, invalidation, resize, reload, disable and teardown
    retire owned storage. Failed generation selects marching and never publishes previous contents.
  Live appearance and native whole-frame performance remain open in Phase 9. Earlier prototype
    timing and source-only delivery hashes above remain historical evidence, not this package's identity.
  Validation -> artifacts/CloudRealtime/phase8/default-cache/ -> focused.trx passes 13 checks for
    bindings, density, source arithmetic and integration. After the final persistent-image ordering
    barrier, production-owner-final.trx passes both PBR cases (2/2), including active default cache,
    generation-factory failure with exact marching fallback, source revocation and resource retirement.
    sparse-pbr-0.trx and sparse-pbr-1.trx each pass the small sparse/grazing fallback/rebuild case.
    These are overlapping focused receipts, not an inflated sum of unique tests. Radiance differences
    remain diagnostic; unchanged optical factors, clipping/support and failure-path arithmetic remain
    correctness checks. The obsolete experimental trace/program wrappers are removed; diagnostics
    use the production shader. Timing environment flags control measurements, not default enablement.
